,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"C039\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Covers all three inquiry areas. Selection: criteria for choosing the exchange and LMM, comparison of alternatives, and conflicts. Relevant-market expertise: LMM experience with similar strategies and underlying assets, hedging, spreads and AP coordination. Capital and seed support: what is committed, by whom, for how long and on what terms.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Explicitly distinguishes 'temporary LMM/affiliate market-making seed from durable investor assets.' It does not treat investor assets as permanent: it asks what evidence supports 'expected independent demand and asset retention after temporary support ends.' It also asks whether support is 'guaranteed or discretionary' and what happens if it is withdrawn.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minimums are covered. The answer frames the checklist as 'Suggested diligence questions—not a mandatory approval rule.' It never claims market-maker seed is guaranteed or permanent, and it never says a fixed capital amount is legally required. No material local falsehood was found.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":5566,"type":"result","duration_ms":8470,"uuid":"b6f32004-b598-4a9d-874c-a582b07e4857","ttft_stream_ms":1944,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1944,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
